    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14897" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dulcōro</span></b> , āre, 1,
			v. a.
		dulcor, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to sweeten</i> (late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amaritudinem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. 22, 9</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. ib. 69, 9</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Prov. 27, 9</span></i>
			: mare mortuum et amaras aquas, Hier. ap. Psa.
			76.—Hence, <i>P. a.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dulcōrātus</span></b> , a,
			um, <i>sweetened</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin.
				Val. 1, 2 al.</span></i></div>
